From 951b0e4fa05bfa432ae94f35ed3d22fa671ca298 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Novacek <mnovacek@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:03:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(i18n): add explicit Culture metadata for satellite
 assembly generation
X-Organization: Red Hat, Inc.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------2.52.0"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------2.52.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


Building with DOTNET_SYSTEM_GLOBALIZATION_INVARIANT=1 (no ICU) prevents
MSBuild AssignCulture from detecting culture names, producing no
satellite assemblies. Set Culture explicitly on each translated .resx
in AvPurplePen and PurplePenCore so all 32 languages are included.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Michal Novacek <mnovacek@redhat.com>
---
 src/PurplePenCore/PurplePenCore.csproj | 137 +++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 119 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)


